{"name":"Tahoe Blue","hex":"#94b8c1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lake Tahoe","blocks":[{"text":"Lake Tahoe is a freshwater lake in the Sierra Nevada of the Western United States, straddling the border between California and Nevada. Lying at 6,225 ft (1,897 m) above sea level, Lake Tahoe is the largest alpine lake in North America, and at 122,160,280 acre⋅ft (150.7 km3) it trails only the five Great Lakes as the largest by volume in the United States. Its depth is 1,645 ft (501 m), making it the second deepest in the United States after Crater Lake in Oregon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Tahoe_North_Shore_from_the_East_Shore.jpg/330px-Tahoe_North_Shore_from_the_East_Shore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Tahoe"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Lake_Tahoe_by_Sentinel-2.jpg/500px-Lake_Tahoe_by_Sentinel-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Lake_Tahoe_by_Sentinel-2.jpg/1280px-Lake_Tahoe_by_Sentinel-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Lake_Tahoe_by_Sentinel-2.jpg/500px-Lake_Tahoe_by_Sentinel-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALake_Tahoe_by_Sentinel-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/North_Lake_Tahoe_Aerial_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/500px-North_Lake_Tahoe_Aerial_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/North_Lake_Tahoe_Aerial_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/1280px-North_Lake_Tahoe_Aerial_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/North_Lake_Tahoe_Aerial_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/500px-North_Lake_Tahoe_Aerial_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"North Lake Tahoe aerial photo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorth_Lake_Tahoe_Aerial_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Lake_Tahoe%2C_view_of_California_from_Nevada_side.jpg/500px-Lake_Tahoe%2C_view_of_California_from_Nevada_side.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi